# Layout grid

Every screen shares one content grid. Header, hero, filters, cards, and footer line up on the same left and right edges.

Tokens and classes live in `src/styles.css`. Do not invent a second width, gutter, or column count.

## Container

- Full-bleed background. Content is one box: `max-width: var(--layout-max)` and `padding-inline: var(--layout-gutter)` on that same element.
- Use `.layout-container`. A page shell may repeat those two declarations. It may not add a third width.
- Horizontal padding goes on the content box only. An outer full-bleed block and an inner `max-width` box do not both get gutter padding.
- Blog and privacy use `.layout-container--prose` (`--layout-prose-max: 760px`). Chrome around them still uses `--layout-max`.
- The staff cabinet (`/admin`, admin and superadmin only) wraps the page in `.layout-staff`. That class sets `--layout-max` to `--layout-staff-max` (`1680px`), so the header, the cabinet, and the footer on those pages share one wider edge. Trainer cabinet, account, and the public catalog stay on `1240px`. Do not put `.layout-staff` on `/trainer-admin` or `/account`.
- Gap between columns and cards is `--layout-gap` (24px). Sidebar is `--layout-sidebar-w` (280px) via `.layout-with-sidebar`.
- A horizontal scroller (icon rail, card rail) uses `.layout-rail`. The track scrolls inside that box. It does not use `100vw` or sit flush with the screen edge.
- `--layout-gutter` already includes `env(safe-area-inset-*)`. The viewport meta keeps `viewport-fit=cover` so a standalone PWA does not draw content under the notch.

## Columns

Shared classes in `src/styles.css`. Do not set `grid-template-columns` on them in a route `<style>` — that block loads later and overrides the global grid.

| Classes | Columns |
| --- | --- |
| `.card-grid`, `.clubs-grid`, `.categories-grid` | 3, then 2 at `960px`, then 1 at `640px` |
| `.card-grid--4`, `.cat-clubs-row`, `.city-districts`, `.trainer-grid`, `.cat-grid`, `.city-grid`, `.sr-grid` | 4, then 2 at `960px`, then 1 at `640px` |
| `.layout-with-sidebar` | `280px + 1fr`, then 1 column at `960px` |

## Do not

- `max-width: 1120px`, `820px`, `1100px`, `1680px`, or any other content width. The only widths are `--layout-max`, `--layout-staff-max`, and `--layout-prose-max`.
- `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(...))` for catalog cards
- A flex-wrap row where the card grid should sit
- Page CSS that resets `.trainer-grid`, `.cat-grid`, or the other shared grids

```css
/* wrong: gutter twice, content shifts left of the header */
.hero { padding-inline: var(--layout-gutter); }
.hero-inner { max-width: var(--layout-max); margin-inline: auto; }

/* right */
.hero { padding-inline: 0; }
.hero-inner { max-width: var(--layout-max); margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: var(--layout-gutter); }
```
